From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: skip only the known unusable Valgrind runtime

License: BSD-3-Clause
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Origin: openEuler RISC-V packaging

The openEuler RVA23 repository provides Valgrind but keeps glibc debuginfo in
a separate repository outside the approved package-build dependency source.
Valgrind therefore exits before running detox because it cannot install its
mandatory strcmp redirection for the stripped RISC-V dynamic loader.

Probe the exact detox binary first.  Skip memory instrumentation only when
Valgrind reports both signatures of that known startup limitation.  Preserve
the failure for every other probe error, and keep the remainder of the issue
56 stress scenario and the complete test suite unchanged.

This was reproduced by exact-head openEuler RISC-V CI run 31761326115.
Remove the patch when the approved target buildroot supplies compatible glibc
debug information or upstream carries an equivalent fail-closed capability
probe.

---
 tests/legacy/github-issue-0056/test.sh | 23 ++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/legacy/github-issue-0056/test.sh b/tests/legacy/github-issue-0056/test.sh
--- a/tests/legacy/github-issue-0056/test.sh
+++ b/tests/legacy/github-issue-0056/test.sh
@@ -34,5 +34,18 @@
-if [ -z "$VALGRIND" ] ; then
-	echo WARNING: valgrind is not installed
-else
-	$VALGRIND --quiet --error-exitcode=1 --track-origins=yes "$DETOX" a b c d e f g h i j k
-fi
+if [ -z "$VALGRIND" ] ; then
+	echo WARNING: valgrind is not installed
+elif PROBE_LOG=$(mktemp) && $VALGRIND --quiet --error-exitcode=1 \
+		"$DETOX" -V >/dev/null 2>"$PROBE_LOG" ; then
+	rm -f "$PROBE_LOG"
+	$VALGRIND --quiet --error-exitcode=1 --track-origins=yes "$DETOX" a b c d e f g h i j k
+else
+	if grep -Fq 'mandatory for this platform-tool combination' "$PROBE_LOG" \
+		&& grep -Fq 'Cannot continue -- exiting now' "$PROBE_LOG" ; then
+		cat "$PROBE_LOG" >&2
+		echo 'SKIP: valgrind cannot instrument the target glibc runtime'
+		rm -f "$PROBE_LOG"
+	else
+		cat "$PROBE_LOG" >&2
+		rm -f "$PROBE_LOG"
+		exit 1
+	fi
+fi
